CREATED:20260415T205337Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a lecture by 2016 Nobel Laureate Dr. Robert
  J. Lefkowitz\, the Chancellor's Distinguished Professor of Medicine and 
 Professor of Biochemistry at Duke University. \n\nLefkowitz studies recep
 tor biology and signal transduction. He is best known for his detailed ch
 aracterizations of the sequence\, structure\, and function of the β-adren
 ergic and related receptors\, and for the discovery and characterization 
 of the two families of proteins that regulate them-the G protein-coupled 
 receptor (GPCR) kinases and β-arrestins.\n\nHis talk\, "G-protein Coupled
  Receptors\," is part of the 2026 Victor J. Dzau Lecture Seminar Series a
 nd is sponsored by The Mandel Center for Hypertension and Atherosclerosis
 .\n\nPhysician Credit: Duke University Health System Department of Clinic
 al Education and Professional Development designates this activity for a 
 maximum of 1 AMA PRA Category 1 Credit(s) TM.  Physicians should claim on
 ly credit commensurate with the extent of their participation in the acti
 vity.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260418T181150Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260527T120000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260418T181150Z
